content.text:
The root cause is the payment service, which went down and never served requests again in the abnormal window. Its failure reaches users through checkout, frontend and frontend-proxy. The product-reviews, AI-assistant and dns.lookup errors also appear in the normal period, so they are baseline and not part of this incident.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "payment",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, count(*) AS n, min(value) AS mn, max(value) AS mx FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'payment%' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Payment container restart counter rose from 1 to 2 during the abnormal window, restarting twice near 03:55-03:56."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n, quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6 AS p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name = 'oteldemo.PaymentService/Charge' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "All 19 checkout calls to PaymentService/Charge error within about 0.02-0.6 ms; payment emits no spans in the abnormal window."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, count(*) AS spans FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'payment' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Payment has zero spans in the abnormal window, versus 32 spans in the normal window."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "payment",
